-- ============================================================================
-- EC2 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Fiscal Regime Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE COMPARISON AND WHAT TO DISTRUST. Six regimes at
-- once, the summary and its sort, the price sweep and progressivity, the
-- capex sweep, the derived insights, and five numbers a careful reader must
-- not take at face value.
--
-- THE TIER IS AN EXERCISE IN READING A SCREEN AGAINST ITS OWN ARITHMETIC.
-- Every one of the five numbers below is returned by the published engine,
-- is agreed with by an independent stdlib oracle, and is pinned in the
-- goldens. None of them is a bug in the sense of a wrong calculation. Each
-- is a case where the number is correct and the LABEL is not, and that is
-- the harder thing to teach and the more useful thing to know.
--
--   THE RATE WITH TWO VALUES. The summary table divides government take by
--   take plus contractor take WITH total capex added back; the price
--   sensitivity divides the same quantities on the same cash flows WITHOUT
--   it. Both are labelled "effective tax rate" and both are on one screen.
--
--   THE CURVE WITH THREE MEANINGS. That same sweep is a share between 0 and
--   100; is above 100 when the contractor is losing money while the
--   government still collects; and is EXACTLY 0 when the guard fires because
--   the denominator was not positive. Six regimes plot a flat zero across
--   the whole sweep on the published never-recovers comparison, each having
--   collected hundreds or thousands of millions of dollars. THE EC2 WAVE
--   FOUND THIS ONE. It is not in the oracle findings file; it is written up
--   in the wave's FINDINGS.md as EC2-1 with the owner's three options.
--
--   THE LABEL THAT IS NOT THE SWEEP. The capex loop runs 0.8 to 1.5 in steps
--   of 0.1, floating point puts the eighth step at 1.5000000000000004, and
--   the sweep has SEVEN points whose last label reads 1.4 under an axis that
--   promises 1.5. The resilience verdict prices a 40 percent overrun.
--
--   THE VERDICT THAT RANKS NOISE. The capex and price insights pick with a
--   strict less-than in a reduce, so an exact tie goes to list order and a
--   tie in the fifteenth figure goes to the smaller rounding error. The
--   engine and the oracle name different winners on the same case and
--   neither is a result.
--
--   THE SOLVER THAT REPORTS ITS OWN EDGE. The bisection brackets by doubling
--   from 100 percent ten times and returns 102400 percent when the NPV is
--   still positive there. The screening engine next door returns its 1000
--   percent Newton clamp. A suspiciously round number where a rate should be
--   is the tell in both.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The summary is sorted by contractor NPV
-- descending, so position in the table means ONE thing and a reader who
-- reads any other ranking off it (fastest payback, most government revenue,
-- most resilient) is reading a claim the sort does not make. That mistake
-- is the reason deriveInsights exists: the Insights tab used to state four
-- conclusions of which three were never computed.
-- ============================================================================

values ('fiscal', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-six-regimes-at-once","title":"Six Regimes at Once","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-comparison-returns","l02-the-summary-and-its-sort","l03-the-effective-tax-rate-in-the-table","l04-payback-and-the-payout-year"]},{"key":"m02-the-price-sweep","title":"The Price Sweep","lesson_keys":["l01-the-swept-range","l02-the-government-share-curve","l03-progressivity","l04-the-multiplier-scales-oil-only","l05-the-second-effective-tax-rate"]},{"key":"m03-the-capex-sweep","title":"The Capex Sweep","lesson_keys":["l01-the-multiplier-loop","l02-the-point-the-loop-never-reaches","l03-what-resilience-measures","l04-two-sweeps-side-by-side","l05-reading-a-verdict-that-moved"]},{"key":"m04-the-insights","title":"The Insights","lesson_keys":["l01-four-claims-that-were-never-computed","l02-how-each-one-is-derived-now","l03-a-tie-ranked-by-noise","l04-when-nothing-pays-back","l05-one-regime-and-none"]},{"key":"m05-numbers-to-distrust","title":"Numbers to Distrust","lesson_keys":["l01-the-rate-with-two-values","l02-the-label-that-is-not-the-sweep","l03-the-irr-that-reports-its-bracket","l04-the-uplift-charged-every-year"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
